In tonight's edition, 15 military officials are sanctioned by the UK over the brutality and abuse of civilians during the fall of El Fasher. Also, ⁠Algeria's set to send in army units ​to ‌Niger ⁠to ‌protect energy ⁠and economic interests there. And days after a foreigner was beaten to death on the streets of Durban, the stalled asylum process has left many migrants living in fear. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c8190e2-d183-11f1-ad8e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006282-VOD-00023652-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c8190e2-d183-11f1-ad8e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006282-VOD-00023652-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80957748-d183-11f1-9ec6-a3934f97f5ba</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:26:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Algeria to send troops to Niger in first foreign deployment in over 50 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261026-algeria-to-send-troops-to-niger-in-first-foreign-deployment-in-over-50-years</link><description>
Algeria’s parliament on Sunday approved a resolution to send troops to Niger, making the first time Algerian soldiers will be deployed abroad since the 1973 Arab-Israeli war. Niger faces persistent attacks by armed groups, including near its border with Algeria, and the deployment comes as Algiers and Niamey are building the Trans-Saharan Gas Pipeline after decades of delays. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec70da56-d120-11f1-8043-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298690018388.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec70da56-d120-11f1-8043-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298690018388.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f578d036-d120-11f1-b522-ff2dd1b862e1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:10:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec70da56-d120-11f1-8043-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298690018388.jpg">© Fateh Guidoum, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Building collapse in Nairobi: Search for survivors under way</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way</link><description>
In tonight's programme: Rescuers comb through rubble in a bid to reach trapped survivors after a multi-storey building under construction in Nairobi collapses. Also, Kenya announces a second Ebola death. Earlier this week it had logged nine cases, all traced back to its first Ebola patient who died earlier this month. Finally, with the 11th edition of the iconic contemporary art festival Also Known as Africa taking place in Paris, we speak to Cape Verdean artist Amadeo Carvalho.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ca47780-cf20-11f1-a61d-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bed663fa.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6ca47780-cf20-11f1-a61d-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bed663fa.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1750ef52-cf20-11f1-996d-211c1872ac14</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:31:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>SA faces rising tension as foreign national is killed amid anti-migrant protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests</link><description>
South African police are investigating the murder of a foreign national after violent protests by anti-immigrant groups swept through the central business district in Durban. The latest death follows months of violent rallies in which at least 10 foreigners were killed and several other countries on the continent raced to repatriate their people. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d03acde-cec3-11f1-9b9e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-214526-214702-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d03acde-cec3-11f1-9b9e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-214526-214702-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">828bb12e-cec3-11f1-8b0b-9b797395f52e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:08:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Across Africa</category><title>Across Africa: Ivorian vinyl head's heritage hunt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt</link><description>
This week in Across Africa: Ivorian music lover Cédric Kouamé is on a mission to restore 20th-century African vinyl and bring old-school sounds back to modern playlists. Also, 10 years after Cameroon's worst railway disaster, families are still fighting for justice for the 79 people killed. Finally, in São Tomé and Príncipe, we discover how the islands' rich volcanic soils produce some of the world's most distinctive vanilla.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8dd2770-cecb-11f1-9d94-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-000d2b86.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8dd2770-cecb-11f1-9d94-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-000d2b86.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">771742aa-ce5e-11f1-9758-156ff0704180</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:27:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>Olympic fever grips Senegal as Dakar hosts Youth Olympic Games</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog</link><description>
As Senegal prepares to host the Youth Olympic Games (YOG), the first Olympic event ever organised in Africa, the country is pulling out all the stops to be ready on time. FRANCE 24’s Sarah Sakho and Simon Martin report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/239dc254-ce1b-11f1-a7da-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-EN-reporters.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/239dc254-ce1b-11f1-a7da-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-EN-reporters.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf59236a-ce1e-11f1-ad2c-6796427f56e6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:58:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Simon MARTIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ivory Coast: Children face serious health risks from lead in paint</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint</link><description><![CDATA[
Across Ivory Coast, teams are going door-to-door, testing homes for dangerous levels of lead as efforts to raise awareness of the toxic metal’s health risks intensify. Report by Jean Barrère & Guillaume Gougeon.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc97410-ceba-11f1-a099-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082335-082547-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bcc97410-ceba-11f1-a099-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082335-082547-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c22a6afe-ceba-11f1-90f8-7fb21b4796f0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:37:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Africa faces 'complex' Ebola outbreak after spread to Nigeria: WHO</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa-faces-complex-ebola-outbreak-after-spread-to-nigeria-who</link><description>
The World Health Organization warned Thursday that Africa faced a "complex" Ebola outbreak after the virus crossed from east Africa to Nigeria, marking the first case in the west of the continent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7e9f0b4-ceba-11f1-9d55-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082125-082315-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7e9f0b4-ceba-11f1-9d55-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261023-082125-082315-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bcae43ca-ceba-11f1-9e94-1f871d4d611b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:28:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>South Africa gripped by anti-migrant protests as foreign national is killed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261023-south-africa-gripped-by-anti-migrant-protests-as-foreign-national-is-killed</link><description>
Xenophobic unrest turns deadly in South Africa as a foreign national is beaten to death during a protest march in Durban, a city increasingly gripped by anti-migrant tensions. Meanwhile, as global efforts to raise awareness of lead poisoning intensify, teams in Ivory Coast go door-to-door testing homes for dangerous levels of the toxic metal. Finally, Ivorian authorities are cracking down on illegal mining over fears of pollution, but some young people say the activity remains one of their few sources of income. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49e20596-ceb7-11f1-b7ca-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-78054085.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49e20596-ceb7-11f1-b7ca-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-78054085.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8400964-ce65-11f1-b3cc-f319924fdc6e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:24:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Ethiopia-Eritrea: Is there a risk of a wider conflict?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261022-ethiopia-eritrea-is-there-a-risk-of-a-wider-conflict</link><description>
Concerns are mounting as Ethiopia and Eritrea inch closer to war. With Ethiopia now having taken control of the border town of Zalambessa, the fear is that Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed will send his troops into Eritrea. In Perspective, we spoke to Martin Plaut, a senior research fellow at the Institute of Commonwealth Studies at the University of London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98b6ee-ce19-11f1-8fb6-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6186ba6e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a98b6ee-ce19-11f1-8fb6-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6186ba6e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ffa2408c-cdf2-11f1-9d41-53ef36ae02a5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:40:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yinka OYETADE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Cameroon: Ten years after a massive train disaster, victims are still awaiting justice</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-cameroon-ten-years-after-a-massive-train-disaster-victims-are-still-awaiting-justice</link><description><![CDATA[
It has been ten years since a Cameroon National Railway Intercity train travelling between Yaounde and Douala derailed and became the country's worst ever railway disaster. Seventy-nine people were killed and hundreds were injured. Report by Indira Ayuk, Richard Tessoh, Giresse Ngaana & Guillaume Gougeon.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/319a19c0-cd76-11f1-be77-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/AP16296707809075.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/319a19c0-cd76-11f1-be77-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/AP16296707809075.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2e40f5c-ce1e-11f1-a178-c9372df3da2e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:23:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Sudan's war escalates as UN warns of wider regional crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261021-sudan-s-war-escalates-as-un-warns-of-wider-regional-crisis</link><description>
In tonight's edition: Sudan's brutal war continues to take a devastating regional toll, as a drone strike in Abyei reportedly kills 153 people. We speak to the UN envoy for Sudan following an emergency international meeting on the escalating crisis. Also, health authorities prepare to coordinate a response as Ebola cases emerge in Nigeria and rise in Kenya. Finally, 10 years after Cameroon’s deadliest railway disaster, families of the 79 victims are still fighting for justice, saying their pain has yet to be acknowledged.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25d330b6-cda0-11f1-942a-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3969bf04.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25d330b6-cda0-11f1-942a-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3969bf04.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc368094-cd9f-11f1-9510-3b56e5302474</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:41:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Neither the Sudanese military, nor the RSF take any acknowledgement of human life in this war'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war</link><description>
The death toll from a drone strike Monday on a market in an area disputed between Sudan and South Sudan has risen to 153 and is likely even higher, a local official told AFP on Wednesday. Authorities in Abyei district said the strike on the Amiet market involved the use of multiple munitions and was carried out by the Sudanese army. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Jan Pospisil, Sudan Affairs Analyst at the Peace and Conflict Resolution Evidence Platform. He says that for a long time the Sudanese army has tried "to portray a picture internationally that they are humane, whereas RSF is committing atrocities. Here we see very clearly that there is not much difference between these two".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/303326fa-cd83-11f1-989f-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-203844-205016-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/303326fa-cd83-11f1-989f-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-203844-205016-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3521d5da-cd83-11f1-ac98-f9a30321d3f0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:28:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya: Trial shows crucial role of religion in Shakahola massacre</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-kenya-trial-shows-crucial-role-of-religion-in-shakahola-massacre</link><description>
The Kenyan cult leader found guilty on Monday of the deaths of 190 children and one adult will be sentenced on November 6th. Paul Mackenzie starved his followers in what became known as the Shakahola massacre. But this trial was about more than just a criminal and his accomplices. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Bastien Renouil.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb376dba-cc01-11f1-9791-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292477298169.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb376dba-cc01-11f1-9791-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292477298169.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07f9b834-cd51-11f1-8c08-29ca1ae5660b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:48:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South African former police chief accused of sex trafficking denied bail</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-south-african-former-police-chief-accused-of-sex-trafficking-denied-bail</link><description>
South Africa's former deputy national commissioner, Shadrack Sibiya, has been denied bail. He is facing charges of rape, trafficking and is accused of sexually grooming a child. Investigators had argued that his accusers would be in danger if he was let out. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3f272878-cd51-11f1-844d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7cd460dc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3f272878-cd51-11f1-844d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7cd460dc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">18493d92-cd4f-11f1-b3a0-1773a65f3b01</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:44:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case amid rapid regional spread</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-amid-rapid-regional-spread</link><description>
After Kenya and Uganda, Nigeria has now announced its first Ebola case – a woman who was admitted to a private hospital in Abuja and travelled from Uganda. The outbreak, which originated in DR Congo in May, has been described by health officials as ​thefastest-spreading on record. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48a63b76-cd53-11f1-9c1d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T045618Z-1772179031-RC2G4OAZODI8-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-NIGERIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48a63b76-cd53-11f1-9c1d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T045618Z-1772179031-RC2G4OAZODI8-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-NIGERIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da5056e4-cd4c-11f1-b5cb-6968c0ef0e51</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:28:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>US sanctions on ICC are 'a shock' and 'unacceptable', Nobel peace laureate Navi Pillay says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261021-us-sanctions-on-icc-are-a-shock-and-unacceptable-nobel-peace-laureate-navi-pillay-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Navi Pillay described the US sanctions imposed on the International Criminal Court (ICC) hours after her award as "a shock" and "unacceptable". The South African judge also defended the UN commission of inquiry she chaired which concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza: "We didn't come to that conclusion lightly." Rejecting claims that the ICC targets Africa, she said "the court is not selective".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36f02c16-cd30-11f1-bde0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-26.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36f02c16-cd30-11f1-bde0-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/Untitled-Sequence-01-26.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38559cb0-cd32-11f1-998a-0996ab77a850</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:11:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigeria records first Ebola case as outbreak spreads across Africa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-nigeria-records-first-ebola-case-as-outbreak-spreads-across-africa</link><description>
Nigeria has confirmed its first Ebola case in Africa's latest outbreak, while Kenya reported its ninth infection, raising fears of further spread across the continent. Africa CDC chief Jean Kaseya warned of an “extremely serious threat” and urged the international community to send funding, medical supplies and health workers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9f009a-cccf-11f1-8fb9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293670227514.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9f009a-cccf-11f1-8fb9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293670227514.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a126bcb6-ccdc-11f1-a98c-278e4208fe9c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:18:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9f009a-cccf-11f1-8fb9-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293670227514.jpg">© Chinedu Asadu, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Nigeria confirms first Ebola case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-confirms-first-ebola-case</link><description>
In tonight's programme: Nigeria confirms its first Ebola case in the midst of an outbreak that began in DR Congo in mid-May. Also, a former top South African police officer facing sexual grooming and rape charges is denied bail. Finally, São Tomé and Príncipe's rich volcanic soils produce vanilla pods with an entrancing taste unlike those grown anywhere else.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d169c3e2-cccc-11f1-897d-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0eb05e6c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d169c3e2-cccc-11f1-897d-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0eb05e6c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9922808c-cccc-11f1-8628-cd2ba0c8870d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:28:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>More than 150 killed in Sudan drone strike on disputed Abyei border region</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-more-than-150-killed-sudan-drone-strike-disputed-abyei-border-region</link><description>
At least 153 people have been killed in a drone strike on a market in the disputed Abyei region, where a fire at a nearby fuel depot continued to burn on Tuesday. Local officials blamed Sudan’s military for Monday’s attack, which also left dozens injured. 
 

 

 

